# Garment Production System — Definitive Implementation Plan

## 1. Goal

Transform the existing 4-component ML prediction system into a complete, full-stack **Garment Production Management Portal** with:
- **Buyer portal** — register, submit requests, track order status
- **Admin portal** — approve accounts, review ML recommendations, assign orders to plants
- **Plant Manager portal** — view assigned orders, submit daily logs, mark orders as ready
- **Email notifications** at every critical lifecycle event
- **Dynamic capacity** — model outputs change automatically as orders fill up factory capacity
- **SQLite DB** backing all state, replacing all hardcoded dicts and Excel files

---

## 2. User Roles & Permissions

| Role | Can Do | Cannot Do |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **Admin** | Approve/reject buyer accounts, view all orders, review C1/C2 recommendations, assign orders to plants, view C4 plant health scores, trigger manual re-analysis | Add new plants, change plant static KPIs |
| **Buyer** | Register, submit sample orders, submit bulk orders (after sample approved), view own order status and history | See other buyers' orders, see plant details |
| **PlantManager** | View assigned orders, submit daily production logs (C3), mark bulk orders as Ready | See other plants' orders, assign orders |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Plants are **pre-seeded** from the dataset — no UI to add new ones. Each plant gets one pre-created PlantManager account. Admins cannot add plants.

