## 4. Model & Dataset Compatibility Audit

### Component 1 — Sample Planning
- **User-provided fields:** `style_number`, `artwork_number`, `sample_qty`, `receive_date`, `buyer_required_date`, `notes`
- **DB-derived (no longer in request):** buyer DOW from `buyers_config`, live capacity from `plant_capacity_history`
- **Hardcoded dicts to migrate:** `BUYER_SHIPMENT_SCHEDULE`, `BUYER_DOW`, `PLANT_QUALITY`, `PLANT_LOCATIONS`, `PLANT_ONTIME_RATES`, `PLANT_UTIL_RANGE`
- **Excel to migrate:** `capacity_full_year_2024.xlsx` + `capacity_full_year_2026.xlsx` → `plant_capacity_history`
- **Models:** `m3_delay_classifier.pkl`, `le_buyer.pkl`, `le_priority.pkl` — **unchanged**

### Component 2 — Bulk Order Planning
- **User-provided fields:** `bulk_order_quantity`, `daily_commitment`, `style_priority`, `design_width`, `design_length`, `color_count`, `stitch_count`, `damage_pct`, `shipment_days`
- **DB-derived (no longer in request):** `monthly_capacity` dict read from `plant_monthly_capacity`, plant quality from `plants` table
- **Hardcoded dicts to migrate:** `QUALITY_MAP`, `ALLOCATION_GUIDE`, `PRIORITY_ENC`, `BUYER_ENC`
- **Models:** `c2_model_cutting.pkl`, `c2_model_sewing.pkl`, `c2_model_embroidery.pkl`, `c2_model_allocation.pkl`, `c2_model_deadline.pkl` — **unchanged**

### Component 3 — Daily Emergency Detection
- **User-provided fields:** `plant_daily_output`, `daily_damage_qty`, `max_daily_damage_qty`, `machine_breakdown_count`, `worker_shortage_count`, `cumulative_completed_qty`
- **DB-derived:** `bulk_order_id`, `full_order_qty`, `daily_commitment`, `total_working_days`, `working_day_no` (auto-counted from log entries), `production_date`
- **Models:** `c3_model1_risk_type.pkl`, `c3_model2_order_risk.pkl` — **unchanged**
- **Trigger:** runs automatically on every daily log submission

### Component 4 — Production Analysis
- **User-provided fields:** `machine_count`, `active_machine_count`, `employee_count`, `daily_output_avg`, `total_workload`, `urgent_style_flag`, `urgent_handled_count`, `machine_breakdown_days`, `worker_shortage_days`, `damage_rate`, `planned_completion_days`, `actual_completion_days`
- **DB-derived:** `risk_count_from_component3` (aggregated from `daily_logs` C3 results), `on_time_rate` + `quality_rating` from `plants` table
- **Hardcoded dicts to migrate:** `PLANT_NAME_TO_ID`, `PLANT_KPI`
- **Models:** `model_A_perf_regressor.pkl`, `model_B_star_classifier.pkl`, `model_D_best_plant.pkl`, `model_E_multilabel_recommendation.pkl`, `scaler.pkl`, `encoders.pkl` — **unchanged**
- **Trigger:** Admin or Plant Manager can run C4 analysis for any bulk order (weekly review)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No ML `.pkl` files change.** The DB only replaces hardcoded dicts and Excel files that feed INTO the models. Feature vectors stay identical.

